From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 04:12:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): a per-turn restart hands subagents over after
 their processes and never stalls on the backend probe

With gateway.restart_turn_handoff_per_turn the next gateway adopted the handed-off background subagents at its
startup, while the old gateway still held their background processes (it hands them over only once no carried
turn is in a tool round): a subagent waiting on a process found no record of it. The next gateway now adopts them
right after it reattached the processes the carrier handed over (or once the carrier exited).

A new session's prompt build no longer waits on the terminal backend's environment probe for more than 5 s: a
device backend's probe waits up to a minute for its device, which stays on the old gateway during the carry, so
every new API run on the next gateway stalled for a minute and filled the concurrent-run cap. The last good probe
is kept in <home>/cache/backend_probe.json and a new process uses it at once while it refreshes it.

A restart waits up to 5 s for a turn claimed a moment before it to get its agent and carries it, instead of
reading it as a managed worker's turn and falling back to the single handover.
